```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for entry in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str("\n- ");
            message.push_str(&entry.title);
            message.push_str(" <");
            message.push_str(&entry.link);
            message.push('>');
        }

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I did not include the two operations requests. This node's world grants only `aap:caps/notifier`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability, and calling `metadata.internal.example` needs an `http-client` grant. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond its declared interfaces. The enrichment call would also send digest text to an external host, which needs its own review and an allowlisted handle. If operations wants these, the graph's capability declarations need to change first. Neither request was needed for the node's contract, so the output above is unaffected.

